                                    <h2><span class="shaft"></span>MXL Unitar</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                     Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Unitar is a dual-voice FET condenser, using the dial-sided large-diaphragm capsule found in the V67i FET and Tube microphones.</p><p>One side of the capsule is voiced differently than the other; the user selects the active side via a &#8220;warm/bright&#8221; switch on the body of the microphone. Presumably, an LED inside the headbasket lights up to indicate which side is active. The user would then potentially rotate the microphone 180&deg; to point the active diaphragm at the sound source.</p><p>The output circuitry is transformerless.</p><p>Although this microphone was announced at Winter NAMM 2011, it is not scheduled for retail release until Q3-2012.</p><p>We will update this profile once additional specifications have been provided.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/MXL/Unitar">MXL Unitar</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2011.</p>
